From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sargo@sargo.cc>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 13:28:02 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 66/67] Plutonium: the switcher's installed shells: an exact
 list from the launcher, customizing and server controls on a shell's page

--plutonium-shells-exact makes --plutonium-shells the whole list, in
order, with "!" before shells that are off; shells it doesn't name are
dropped. The launcher passes its installed shells (~/.pluto/shells.json).

A shell's page in the switcher asks the helper for its installed shells
(GET /v1/shells, polled with the shell states) and, for the one on the
shell's origin, shows a Customize section (Ask an agent, Open a terminal:
a backup terminal tab in its folder; History, log and updates: the
helper's page in the backup browser), any notice of a rolled back
change, and for a server Plutonium runs its state, command and log with
Start/Restart/Stop. Add a shell links to the helper's page for installing
one from a folder, a git URL or an address.

The switcher also turns on shells added on the helper's shells page: GET
/v1/shells marks one ("add"), and the switcher, when it's open, adds it
to the browser's list if no shell is on its origin yet.
